**Must-fix (ranked).** MF-1 (blocker) no tensor definition for the `variant × memory_kind` 4-cell grid — §8.3 fixes real memory to `real_prefix_t` regardless of variant, yet §8.4/§8.5 demand both variants pass, so the grid may be degenerate and `M_PASS_POS`/`M_PASS_NORM` may be the same test twice. MF-2 (blocker) `tail_driven` input omits `variant` although it is a hard B0-B gate. MF-3 (blocker) `P_VALID`/`PA_VALID` cohort unpinned (15 `common_ids` vs 20 native) while it drives `control_status`. MF-4 (blocker) replay hash domain/count ambiguous (600 vs 720 per arm-seed) and the "prelaunch debug vs postrun final" comparison mixes a D1 seed-20261111 hash with the registered run. MF-5 (high) bind `l_copy_signal`/`l_full_signal`. MF-6 (medium) define "full-K" (preflight's excluded set is the nine *longest* val docs, not a `h_len ≥ K` set). MF-7…MF-13 low: control_status wording, availability-NA collapse, `documents_positive`, §12 tail caveat (P0's `.4862` is the *signed* share; the gate's absolute share is `.4335`, ≈`.455` on the 15), fixture defaults, D1 wording, golden digests.

**Verdict: NARROW.** r3.4 freeze: no — text-only r3.5 (=v1.0) closing MF-1…MF-5 first. Implementation + unit tests + D0: conditional after that freeze. D1, 3-seed: not approved. Max compute now: 0; afterwards exactly §10.5 (1,200 updates/120 min registered + D0 0/≤15 min + D1 4/≤20 min = 1,204/155 min, not a grant). test 163 sealed, P1 unused, T5Gemma2 D-108 STOP, Phase 6/B0-B/B1/B2/Stage C not approved.
